## The Section this Leg sits in

A Section is a grouping of Legs under one heading — one promise to the reader
that the question changes here. This Leg either opens a Section or continues
one, and the line below says which. Where it continues, the heading is already
on the page and you are writing further into it: do not restate the heading's
claim, and do not open a new subject.

{{#if section_placement.derived}}
{{#if section_placement.untitled}}
{{#if section_placement.opens}}
- **This Leg OPENS the article's one Section.** This Brief declares no Section titles, so no heading is rendered above your prose.
{{else}}
- **This Leg CONTINUES the article's one Section.** This Brief declares no Section titles, so no heading is rendered, and prose you are writing further into sits above.
{{/if}}
{{else}}
{{#if section_placement.opens}}
- **This Leg OPENS a Section.** Its heading is **"{{section_placement.title}}"**, rendered by the Harness immediately above your prose.
- **Your prose is what the heading promises.** {{#if section_placement.whole}}This Leg is the whole Section.{{else}}{{#if section_placement.one_further}}1 further Leg continues under it, so open the question rather than closing it.{{else}}{{section_placement.further}} further Legs continue under it, so open the question rather than closing it.{{/if}}{{/if}}
{{else}}
- **This Leg CONTINUES the Section headed "{{section_placement.title}}".** That heading is already on the page, above prose you are writing further into.
- **No new heading is rendered here.** Develop what the Section has established; a new subject belongs to a Leg that opens its own.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{else}}
(no Section could be derived for this Leg.)
{{/if}}

{{#if reader_target_line.reaches}}
This Leg reaches the Reader target.
{{else}}
{{#if reader_target_line.closing}}
This Leg follows the Reader target: introduce nothing, raise nothing, and move only what the reader asks, expects or trusts.
{{else}}

{{/if}}
{{/if}}

## What crosses into this Leg

